  "id": "scientist-practitioner-model",
  "term": "scientist-practitioner model",
  "definition": "The scientist-practitioner model is an approach to psychology training in which undergraduate study emphasizes the scientific principles of the discipline, while professional skills are developed later in graduate training. In this model, psychology education is grounded first in research and theory, with applied practice built on that foundation.",
